    "turn_text": "of things I think we should move on from and dispense with race-based decision-making for one. And other things that I think need to have a little bit more of a half-life that we need to remember, remember what the Democratic Socialists have done to us, and would do to us again, given the power to do so. The importance of memory is so crucial in politics. It's so crucial in philosophy. Memory is at the heart of everything. It's at the heart of redemption. It's at the heart. If you're talking theology, it's at the heart of it's at the heart of advancement. If you're thinking in public policy, have we tried it before? Did it work? Have we tried it before? Did it fail? And we live in such a frenzied memory hold moment that we don't have that ability to think on these things anymore. So we just kind of jump from lily pad to lily pad, experimenting. And what it was that Jeff Goldblum said in Jurassic Park, the follow up, the sequel, he said when he was told that they had figured out all the old problems, he said, great. So you're now off to starting a whole bunch of new ones, you know?",
